    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">In twentieth-century America, a land of boundless opportunity, a legendary financier emerged—Charles Ponzi. Rising from pennilessness to overnight wealth, he didn’t stop there. Like a vulture, he swooped in to acquire banks, meddled in Polish bonds, bid for the national fleet, and even attempted to rewrite the rules of finance. Hailed as a “financial maverick” of his time and “the greatest Italian alive,” even the President of the United States once sought to bask in his glory. Yet, not even Ponzi himself knew when this grand dream would come crashing down...</marc:subfield>
